# RoT DTD GOAL -- what must never enter the repository.
#
# The first entry is the important one. `.claude/goal/` is LIVE STATE: the
# criteria of whatever goal is running, the ledger, the timings, the journal,
# the output of every verify command. It is per-session and per-machine. A
# release once swept a stale copy of it into an archive; a stranger cloning
# that would inherit someone else's half-finished goal and a ledger sealed
# against files they do not have.
.claude/goal/
.claude/goal
**/.claude/goal/

# Working scratch produced by the engine and its tests.
*.tmp
*.gfnew
*.pre-*.bak
queue-advance.err

# Release staging. The archive is built by CI from `git archive`, never by hand
# and never committed.
/dist/
*.zip

# EVIDENCE/ IS COMMITTED, DELIBERATELY, and is NOT listed here.
# It carries the differential runs, both mutation logs, the flake-policy
# experiment, the bench, the dogfood journal and ledger, the Lean instrument
# transcript and the Lean sources themselves. A plugin that asks to be trusted
# with the Stop hook owes the reader the material it was judged on -- including
# the runs that went badly. Nothing about how this was verified is withheld.

# The Lean working directory is NOT shipped from here: the modules live in the
# author's Mathlib workspace, and the copies that a reader can check are under
# EVIDENCE/lean/. Ignoring this path keeps a stray local build from shipping
# twice under two names.
/lean/

# Tool caches, session state and agent scratch -- none of it is the plugin.
.claude/
.codemap/
.rot-moe/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Lean build output (the sources ship; the artefacts do not).
.lake/
build/
*.olean
*.ilean
